## Coding Summary (v4)

- **Dominant codes:** `D1.2 > Attack_on_Experts_and_Technocrats`, `D1.3 > Anti_Socialism_Anti_Collectivism`.
- **Sub-dimension balance:** D1.1 (0), D1.2 (1), D1.3 (1). This is an almost entirely technical monetary-theory lecture delivered to a specialist Central Bank audience — one of the most repetitive speeches coded so far, restating nearly the identical theoretical framework (money demand as a "parámetro profundo," dinero exógeno/endógeno, the déficit cero/emisión cero policy sequence) already coded at length in the 2024-09-06 IAEF Mendoza speech.
- **New inductive categories added:** none.
- **Notable rhetorical moves:** The Guillermo Moreno passage is a rare instance of the "bad economic theory" attack directed at a specific named individual former official (rather than a diffuse "econochantas" class), giving it slightly more evidentiary specificity than the recurring generic insults.
